      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chester_Heights%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A railroad first ran through Chester Heights on Christmas Day 1833, sparking a cluster of houses along the new line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chester_Heights%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1836 Logtown School on Valleybrook Road later became Chester Heights School in 1880, now replaced by a newer stone building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
